/*
 ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
 ║        PooKooli Fountain X V2.2  (ESP32-DevKitC)          ║
 ║   V1.0 graduated from the BETA test track after every     ║
 ║   module was verified working individually and together.  ║
 ║   V2.0 was a full redesign: sidebar dashboard web app plus ║
 ║   two new real subsystems — time-of-day Schedule and a     ║
 ║   Recent Activity log.                                     ║
 ║   V2.1 added persistent boot/crash diagnostics — reset     ║
 ║   reason + free heap logged to FLASH every boot (survives  ║
 ║   the crash itself, unlike the RAM activity log), plus a   ║
 ║   min-free-heap tracker, both surfaced on Device Info.      ║
 ║   V2.2 fixes a CONFIRMED crash root cause, found via V2.1's ║
 ║   own boot log: esp_task_wdt_init() was silently failing   ║
 ║   ("already initialized" — newer cores auto-start a        ║
 ║   default watchdog), so our intended 10s timeout never     ║
 ║   actually applied. The I2C auto-recovery sequence then    ║
 ║   outran whatever shorter default WAS active, triggering a ║
 ║   real watchdog panic/reboot mid-recovery. Fixed by         ║
 ║   deiniting any pre-existing watchdog before arming our     ║
 ║   own, plus feeding the watchdog during both the automatic ║
 ║   and manual I2C recovery sequences as defense in depth.    ║
 ║                                                          ║
 ║  VERSIONING:                                             ║
 ║   BETA Vx.y  — test track: +0.1 per module added          ║
 ║   X    Vx.y  — complete edition: +0.1 small, +1.0 big     ║
 ║                                                          ║
 ║   Modules included in this build:                         ║
 ║    ✓ 2× VL53L0X laser sensors (Adafruit lib, XSHUT,       ║
 ║      addr 0x30/0x31), distance range 5–70 cm both         ║
 ║    ✓ Water sensor — real ADC readings, test mode optional ║
 ║    ✓ MOSFET pump (LEDC PWM, 10 power levels)              ║
 ║    ✓ 0.96" OLED (SSD1306) — status + live cm readout      ║
 ║    ✓ Touch sensor (capacitive, active-HIGH) — universal   ║
 ║      manual override: stops any run, or starts a timed    ║
 ║      touch-triggered run                                  ║
 ║    ✓ Web app: sidebar dashboard (Dashboard / Water Tank /  ║
 ║      Pump Control / Schedule / Settings / Device Info /    ║
 ║      Logs) — collapses to a slide-in drawer on phones      ║
 ║    ✓ Schedule: NTP-synced daily trigger times (up to 8),   ║
 ║      persisted to flash, routed through the same           ║
 ║      startPump()/triggerBlocked() path as every other      ║
 ║      trigger source — no separate safety logic             ║
 ║    ✓ Recent Activity log: last 15 events (RAM ring         ║
 ║      buffer, cleared on reboot) — pump start/stop/blocked, ║
 ║      settings saved, system on/off, I2C recovery           ║
 ║    ✓ Device Info page: WiFi/IP/RSSI/MAC, uptime, free      ║
 ║      heap, chip model/rev, firmware version                ║
 ║    ✓ Real photo header + favicon + "Add to Home Screen"   ║
 ║      PWA icon — served directly from the ESP32            ║
 ║    ✓ DEBUG: boot connectivity check + live distances     ║
 ║      shown on the web app AND Serial monitor              ║
 ║    ✓ I2C bus recovery: automatic on sensor dropout, plus  ║
 ║      a manual "Recover I2C Bus" button in the web app     ║
 ║    ✓ Hardware watchdog + NVS-saved settings               ║
 ║    ✓ Laser-triggered pump renews its timer while the cat  ║
 ║      stays in range, instead of stopping mid-drink,       ║
 ║      with a hard 5-minute safety cap regardless           ║
 ║                                                          ║
 ║   NOT included: 433MHz remote (YK04+PT2272-M4) — removed  ║
 ║   during BETA testing after confirmed real electrical     ║
 ║   noise that survived an antenna, a hold filter, and      ║
 ║   dropping the noisiest button. Web app control (WiFi,    ║
 ║   error-checked) proved more robust than RF fighting      ║
 ║   motor EMI.                                              ║
 ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

 ── LIBRARIES  (Arduino Library Manager) ────────────────────
   • Adafruit VL53L0X       — search "VL53L0X" by Adafruit
     (pulls in Adafruit BusIO as a dependency)
   • Adafruit SSD1306        (by Adafruit)
   • Adafruit GFX            (by Adafruit)
   Board: "ESP32 Dev Module"  by Espressif

 ── WIRING ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
  VL53L0X sensor #1:  VCC→3.3V  GND→GND  SDA→GPIO21  SCL→GPIO22
                       XSHUT→GPIO32  (reassigned to addr 0x30 at boot)
  VL53L0X sensor #2:  VCC→3.3V  GND→GND  SDA→GPIO21  SCL→GPIO22
                       XSHUT→GPIO33  (reassigned to addr 0x31 at boot)
  Water level sensor:  GND→GND  +→3.3V  S→GPIO34  (ADC1 ch6)
                       Calibrate WATER_ADC_DRY/WATER_ADC_FULL below to
                       your actual sensor before trusting the % reading
  OLED 0.96" SSD1306:  VCC→3.3V  GND→GND  SDA→GPIO21  SCL→GPIO22
                       (shares I2C bus with both sensors — no extra pins)
  Touch sensor:        VCC→3.3V  GND→GND  SIG→GPIO13
                       (active-HIGH output — no pull-up needed)
  MOSFET module:       Control GND→GND     PWM→GPIO26
 ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*/

